          "snippet": "The Knowledge Argument, primarily formulated by Frank Jackson using the thought experiment of Mary the neurophysiologist, claims that physicalism is false because it cannot account for all facts about consciousness. The reasoning posits that although Mary possesses complete physical knowledge regarding color vision while isolated in a black-and-white room, she acquires new non-physical knowledge upon experiencing color for the first time after her release. This distinction between physical and phenomenal concepts supports the conclusion that not all information is physical."
