          "url": null,
          "score": 0.6360999,
          "snippet": "Husserl’s phenomenology analyzes intentional consciousness by distinguishing between propositional meanings, indexical contents anchored to a determinable X, and the noematic quality of experiences. Through methods like epoché and reduction, he investigates how perceptual singularity and time-consciousness structure experience while bracketing existence assumptions. Furthermore, intersubjective empathy is posited as fundamental for constituting both the objective self-image and the shared spatio-temporal world."
        },
