          "corpus_id": "raptor-subset-on",
          "title": "raptor-subset-on",
          "url": null,
          "score": 0.6306352,
          "snippet": "Husserl develops transcendental phenomenology to analyze the essential structures of consciousness, employing methods such as eidetic reduction and various forms of epoché to bracket naive assumptions. He reconstructs his theory as a non-naive externalist view where intentional content is constituted through dynamic processes involving hyletic data, kinesthetic syntheses, and self-determination within social contexts. Ultimately, he argues for realism by linking the existence of objects to their necessary correlation with subjects capable of acquiring knowledge."
